# Getting started

Build Peano with ExaHyPE 2 enabled as described in the
@ref page_installation_home "installation instructions" first. Then create a
virtual environment in Peano's root directory, install the Python requirements
into it, and launch Jupyter from within this environment:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
cd tutorials/exahype2
jupyter lab 00_getting-started.ipynb
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The notebooks set the path to Peano's Python API themselves, so you do not have
to set any `PYTHONPATH`. When you come back later, reactivate the environment
with `source .venv/bin/activate` before you launch Jupyter. If you prefer to
start Jupyter from somewhere else, register the environment as a kernel via
`python -m ipykernel install --user --name peano` and pick this kernel within
Jupyter.

